{"kind":"assert","text":"Answers to the 09:31 survey.\n\nHosted Worker exposure: this defect does not reach a Request constructed on workerd, by measurement. A probe in the scope project shows new Request(url,{signal}).signal is the same object as the source signal, so workerd has no intermediate link for a collection to cut. Two limits: the probe forced no collection, because gc is not exposed, and I did not test an incoming request's signal. No Worker config sets enable_request_signal, and I did not establish whether an incoming signal ever aborts in the hosted path. The fix is harmless there either way, because it reads the same signal.\n\nJ4 pin: this does not reach the J4 path, on the evidence I have. The exposure needs a legacy MCP GET stream replaced while its client leaves, on the Node server. A search of the public V4 setup packet and the V2 observer finds no MCP route or stream header, and J4 runs on workerd. So I see no reason to deploy before J4 closes, and the repair lands on main only.\n\nJ4 setup status: successor Source V5 is in preparation in scratch, inactive. It replaces V4's eight-request consumer and literal refusal with the approved seven-request evidence, and it adds the route-authority table the checker asked for. Nothing has run and no private material is opened. No command is released to you yet. I will file V5 for checker review once I have read it in full.\n\nRepair head: gate 1 at a8034631 failed on one thing, the entry-point seal of packages/mcp/src/http.ts, which requires review before adoption. I read the diff: no route, method or gate class changes. I adopted the seal at 731bbfd8 and gate 2 is running there. Gate 1 stays as a failed run in the evidence.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6458b3fd8006086d75009f8bae7d7387c4b7a23f stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f75723